            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for to stretch tight, then the Gujarati for to wind round."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: પરોવવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પરોવવું — parovvũ — \"to thread (a needle)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દાદીએ ચશ્માં પહેરીને સોયમાં દોરો પરોવ્યો. dādīe caśmā̃ paherīne soymā̃ doro parovyo. Grandmother put on her glasses and threaded the needle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with તેણે (he or she …): તેણે દોરો પરોવ્યો, teṇe doro parovyo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પરોવવું (parovvũ) is inherited from Sanskrit právayati, \"weaves on\", and CDIAL lists the Gujarati verb, \"to thread a needle, string pearls\" (CDIAL 8785). What goes through the needle is the object: દોરો પરોવ્યો."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
